#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/15_kadi_of_preveza/mission.tres data/missions/35_peace_of_rijeka/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain, for your courage you get the medal of the Bird Dog!"
msgstr ""
"{crew|Capitano|Capitana|Capitani|Capitane}, per il vostro coraggio ricevete la medaglia del Bird "
"Dog!"

#. the title of a mission, on its card
#: data/missions/15_kadi_of_preveza/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Kadı of Preveza"
msgstr "Il cadì di Preveza"

#. the summary of a mission, one or two short sentences
#: data/missions/15_kadi_of_preveza/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring the ledger and the witnesses to the judge in Preveza, then sail home to Pula."
msgstr "Portate il registro e i testimoni al giudice di Preveza, poi tornate a casa a Pula."

#. a fun fact at the end of a mission, at most three sentences
#: data/missions/15_kadi_of_preveza/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"In the Ottoman Empire, a kadı judged by the law, and the people could bring a complaint even "
"against a powerful aga."
msgstr ""
"Nell'Impero ottomano un cadì giudicava secondo la legge, e la gente poteva presentare un reclamo "
"perfino contro un aga potente."

#. the headline of the screen at the end of a mission, a few words
#: data/missions/15_kadi_of_preveza/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The voyage is complete!"
msgstr "Il viaggio è compiuto!"

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/15_kadi_of_preveza/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Aga gave back the double taxes, and the villages are free."
msgstr "L'Aga ha restituito le tasse doppie, e i villaggi sono liberi."

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/15_kadi_of_preveza/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The bell of Grebaštica rings, and the whole Arena of Pula cheers!"
msgstr "La campana di Grebaštica suona, e tutta l'Arena di Pula fa festa!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain, a pigeon came from Bari, with a letter from Luka, the ship's boy!"
msgstr ""
"{crew|Capitano|Capitana|Capitani|Capitane}, è arrivato un piccione da Bari, con una lettera di "
"Luka, il mozzo!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "He writes: \"A Count has come to Italy, Count Malvento. He shows a Golden Charter.\""
msgstr "Scrive: «È arrivato in Italia un Conte, il Conte Malvento. Mostra una Carta d'Oro.»"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "\"He takes a toll in every harbour, from Comacchio to Otranto!\""
msgstr "«Prende un pedaggio in ogni porto, da Comacchio a Otranto!»"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "\"His men even took the eel nets of Comacchio as a toll. Please help!\""
msgstr ""
"«I suoi uomini hanno preso come pedaggio perfino le reti da anguille di Comacchio. Aiutateci!»"

#. what the crew asks, or what the crew is asked
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Have you seen the Count's men with the eel nets?"
msgstr "Avete visto gli uomini del Conte con le reti da anguille?"

#. what the crew asks, or what the crew is asked
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Which boat is the Count's? Remember its sail and its hull!"
msgstr "Qual è la barca del Conte? Ricordate la vela e lo scafo!"

#. a line after a wrong pick
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres data/missions/26_caps_too_new/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "No, not this one! Think of the sail and the hull."
msgstr "No, non questa! Pensate alla vela e allo scafo."

#. a line after the right pick
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"That's the one! The Count's men shrug: \"The Count says nets are a toll.\" But they give them "
"back."
msgstr ""
"È proprio quella! Gli uomini del Conte alzano le spalle: «Il Conte dice che le reti sono un "
"pedaggio.» Ma le restituiscono."

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring the eel nets home to {port}."
msgstr "Riportate le reti da anguille a casa, {port@to}."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Our nets! Now we can catch the eels again."
msgstr "Le nostre reti! Ora possiamo di nuovo pescare le anguille."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Tonight, the whole lagoon eats eels!"
msgstr "Stasera tutta la laguna mangia anguille!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "But this Count... Nobody here ever heard of him before."
msgstr "Ma questo Conte... Qui nessuno ne aveva mai sentito parlare."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Who is he really, captain?"
msgstr "Chi è davvero, {crew|capitano|capitana|capitani|capitane}?"

#. the title of a mission, on its card
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Nets of Comacchio"
msgstr "Le reti di Comacchio"

#. the summary of a mission, one or two short sentences
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The first crossing to Italy. The Count's men took the eel nets of Comacchio \"as a toll\". Follow "
"their boat and give the nets back."
msgstr ""
"La prima traversata verso l'Italia. Gli uomini del Conte hanno preso le reti da anguille di "
"Comacchio «come pedaggio». Seguite la loro barca e riportate le reti."

#. a fun fact at the end of a mission, at most three sentences
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The eels of Comacchio are born far away, in the Sargasso Sea across the ocean, and swim all the "
"way to the lagoon. Nobody knew it in 1600: it was found out only around 1920."
msgstr ""
"Le anguille di Comacchio nascono lontano, nel Mar dei Sargassi al di là dell'oceano, e nuotano "
"fino alla laguna. Nel 1600 nessuno lo sapeva: lo si scoprì solo verso il 1920."

#. the headline of the screen at the end of a mission, a few words
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The nets are home!"
msgstr "Le reti sono a casa!"

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "You crossed the sea and found the Count's boat."
msgstr "Avete attraversato il mare e trovato la barca del Conte."

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The eel fishers of Comacchio can fish again."
msgstr "I pescatori di anguille di Comacchio possono pescare di nuovo."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/17_wind_seller/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain, the Count sells \"wind charms\" to the fishermen of this coast."
msgstr ""
"{crew|Capitano|Capitana|Capitani|Capitane}, il Conte vende «amuleti del vento» ai pescatori di "
"questa costa."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/17_wind_seller/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "He says that without his charm, no boat gets a good wind!"
msgstr "Dice che senza il suo amuleto nessuna barca trova buon vento!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/17_wind_seller/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring me three charms, from Rimini, Fano and Ancona. Let us see what is inside."
msgstr "Portatemi tre amuleti, da Rimini, Fano e Ancona. Vediamo che cosa c'è dentro."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/17_wind_seller/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Here, take my charm. Three ducats, and still no wind!"
msgstr "Ecco, prendete il mio amuleto. Tre ducati, e il vento non c'è lo stesso!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/17_wind_seller/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "It is only a little bottle with a cork."
msgstr "È solo una boccetta con un tappo."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/17_wind_seller/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "My husband paid two ducats for this charm."
msgstr "Mio marito ha pagato due ducati per questo amuleto."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/17_wind_seller/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Shake it: nothing inside! Take it."
msgstr "Scuotetelo: dentro non c'è niente! Prendetelo."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/17_wind_seller/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Count's men sold it to me on the pier."
msgstr "Gli uomini del Conte me l'hanno venduto sul molo."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/17_wind_seller/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Take it, captain. It never helped me."
msgstr "Prendetelo, {crew|capitano|capitana|capitani|capitane}. Non mi è mai servito."

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/17_wind_seller/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Collect {count} more wind {count|charm|charms}."
msgstr "Raccogliete ancora {count} {count|amuleto|amuleti} del vento."

#. what a rival says when he dares the crew to a race, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/17_wind_seller/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Ha! So you collected my wind charms?"
msgstr "Ah! Così avete raccolto i miei amuleti del vento?"

#. what a rival says when he dares the crew to a race, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/17_wind_seller/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "My yellow boat has the best charm of all. Nobody beats it!"
msgstr "La mia barca gialla ha l'amuleto migliore di tutti. Nessuno la batte!"

#. what a rival says when he dares the crew to a race, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/17_wind_seller/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Race me around the three buoys, in front of the fishermen of Fano!"
msgstr "Sfidatemi in regata intorno alle tre boe, davanti ai pescatori di Fano!"

#. what a rival says before a rematch of a race, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/17_wind_seller/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Back for more? The wind still loves me!"
msgstr "Ancora qui? Il vento mi ama ancora!"

#. what a rival says before a rematch of a race, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/17_wind_seller/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Again, around the three buoys!"
msgstr "Di nuovo, intorno alle tre boe!"

#. what the crew hears after winning a race, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/17_wind_seller/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "What? You beat my charm boat?"
msgstr "Cosa? Avete battuto la mia barca portafortuna?"

#. what the crew hears after winning a race, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/17_wind_seller/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bah! The wind was... wrong today."
msgstr "Bah! Oggi il vento era... sbagliato."

#. what the crew hears after winning a race, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/17_wind_seller/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The fishermen of Fano cheer: skill wins, not charms!"
msgstr "I pescatori di Fano esultano: vince la bravura, non gli amuleti!"

#. what the crew hears when a rival won the race, one short sentence
#: data/missions/17_wind_seller/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Ha! The wind loves me! The fishermen ask for a rematch tomorrow."
msgstr "Ah! Il vento mi ama! I pescatori chiedono la rivincita domani."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/17_wind_seller/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Skill wins, not charms! Nobody in Fano buys a wind charm any more."
msgstr "Vince la bravura, non gli amuleti! A Fano nessuno compra più amuleti del vento."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/17_wind_seller/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "We opened them all: empty bottles, every one!"
msgstr "Li abbiamo aperti tutti: boccette vuote, tutte quante!"

#. the title of a mission, on its card
#: data/missions/17_wind_seller/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Wind Seller"
msgstr "Il venditore di vento"

#. the summary of a mission, one or two short sentences
#: data/missions/17_wind_seller/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Collect three wind charms, then race the Count's charm-boat in front of the fishermen of Fano: "
"skill against charms."
msgstr ""
"Raccogliete tre amuleti del vento, poi sfidate la barca del Conte davanti ai pescatori di Fano: "
"bravura contro amuleti."

#. a fun fact at the end of a mission, at most three sentences
#: data/missions/17_wind_seller/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"On the old sea charts of the Mediterranean, the compass rose names eight winds: Tramontana, Greco,"
" Levante, Scirocco, Ostro, Libeccio, Ponente and Maestro. That is how the sailors told the "
"directions."
msgstr ""
"Sulle antiche carte nautiche del Mediterraneo, la rosa dei venti ha otto venti: Tramontana, Greco,"
" Levante, Scirocco, Ostro, Libeccio, Ponente e Maestro. Così i marinai indicavano le direzioni."

#. the headline of the screen at the end of a mission, a few words
#: data/missions/17_wind_seller/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Skill beats charms!"
msgstr "La bravura batte gli amuleti!"

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/17_wind_seller/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "You won the race without a single charm."
msgstr "Avete vinto la regata senza nessun amuleto."

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/17_wind_seller/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The fishermen of Fano keep their ducats now."
msgstr "Ora i pescatori di Fano si tengono i loro ducati."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/18_pilgrims_of_loreto/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain, pilgrims from Pescara want to visit the Holy House of Loreto."
